# `count_distinct`, `count_of` and `contains` with the value recorded, -0.0
# beside 0.0, and a String slot -- see fixtures/160_series_value_reads.ds.
# `CF` reads `count_of(f.v, 0.0)` and `contains(f.v, 0.0)`; `CS` the same for
# "error":
#
#   pump 1  cold: 0, 0, false
#   pump 2  [-0.0]: 1, 1, true;  [error]: 1, 1, true
#   pump 3  [-0.0, 1.0]: 2, 1, true;  [error, ok]: 2, 1, true
#   pump 4  [-0.0, 1.0, 0.0]: 2, 2, true;  [error, ok, error]: 2, 2, true
#
# A bitwise equality reads pump 2's Float row as 1, 0, false. Every assert
# changes its value, so each is a sample ([LFAC.2.5.1]).
# @spec [LSER.16.5.1] [LSER.16.6.1] [LSER.16.7.1]
assert CF k=a v=-0.0
assert CS k=a tag=error
pump
assert CF k=a v=1.0
assert CS k=a tag=ok
pump
assert CF k=a v=0.0
assert CS k=a tag=error
pump
assert CF k=a v=2.0
assert CS k=a tag=warn
pump
